From 61177d95ee610124767ca973a10fc67962794cce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:31:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 211/230] Part: fast interference check for many parts
 (Part.findInterferences, --interference)

  FreeCADCmd model.FCStd --interference [--interference-report pairs.json]

prints every pair of visible solids that overlap, with the common volume.
Python: Part.findInterferences(shapes, tolerance=0, minVolume=1e-6,
threads=0, stats=False) -> [(i, j, volume)], PartViews.interference(doc).

Bounding boxes (BRepBndLib::AddOptimal, sweep and prune along x) pick the
candidate pairs; only those get BRepAlgoAPI_Common and a volume, spread over
all cores with per-thread copies of the shapes (booleans may add pcurves to
their arguments).  A failed boolean is reported with volume -1 instead of
being taken as clear.  Touching parts (zero volume) are not reported.

300 parts (boards, posts, pipes; 87 clashes) on this 15 W laptop:
naive all pairs 44850 booleans 106.5 s, this 1.2 s (2.1 s single thread),
same pairs and volumes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
